  "pages": [
    {
      "type": "spotlight",
      "item": "tribalpower:ward_drum",
      "text": [
        "A camp's night watch. The Ward Drum spends Pulse to strike and shove one hostile at a time, so a creeper never reaches your door. It never targets players."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "What it hits",
      "text": [
        "On each beat, once a second, it finds one hostile within **8 blocks** (a cube around the drum) and hits it for **4 magic damage** with a shove away from the drum.",
        "Each strike costs **8 Pulse** from the lattice. Ranking shortens the beat; Pulse per strike stays 8. It answers to **Spirit**: keep a Spirit totem within 8 blocks (see [Camp hands](camp_hands)), or it stands idle.",
        "Any hostile counts, the overworld's as well as the March's: zombies, skeletons, creepers, spiders, phantoms, witches, drowned and the rest. Players are never the target, and neither are villagers, bonded familiars, yours or anyone's, nor young ones. Bosses shrug it off: the Wither, the Ender Dragon and the March's guardians are left to you."
      ]
    },
